1. Login to App Server 2

From the jump host:

ssh stapp02

Check the OS:

cat /etc/os-release


2. Install Docker CE

If App Server 2 is CentOS/RHEL/Rocky/AlmaLinux, run:

sudo dnf install -y dnf-plugins-core
sudo dnf config-manager --add-repo https://download.docker.com/linux/centos/docker-ce.repo
sudo dnf install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-buildx-plugin docker-compose-plugin


3. Start Docker
sudo systemctl start docker


Enable it at boot:
sudo systemctl enable docker


4. Verify
sudo systemctl status docker

You should see:
Active: active (running)

Then:

docker --version
docker compose version
If the task specifically says "docker compose package"

On modern Docker installations, Docker Compose V2 is provided as:

docker-compose-plugin

and you use it as:

docker compose version

Complete command sequence:

sudo dnf install -y dnf-plugins-core && sudo dnf config-manager --add-repo https://download.docker.com/linux/centos/docker-ce.repo && sudo dnf install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-buildx-plugin docker-compose-plugin && sudo systemctl enable --now docker

If stapp02 gives you an error with any command, paste the error here and I'll give you the exact fix.
